From: EglantinePS5
Subject: up: pipeline lists: export this console's pipeline records without code, import another console's (EDEN_UP_PIPELINE_LIST_EXPORT / EDEN_UP_PIPELINE_LIST_IMPORT), off by default

What: a pipeline list is a console's pipeline records (vulkan.bin, vulkan_mesh.bin) with the
game's code taken out: per record its kind, its key (six program hashes and the 1,008 bytes of
drawing state) and, per program, the CityHash64 of its code and the environment's other bytes
(code size, answers, program header). Format "EGPLIST1" 1: a 32-byte header (format, cache
version 23, key sizes 1056 and 24, record count), then per record u8 kind (0 compute, 1
graphics, 2 task/mesh with mesh state), u8 program count, u16 0, per program u64 code hash, u32
size and the bytes, then the key. tools/pipeline-list.py writes the same bytes on the Mac.

EDEN_UP_PIPELINE_LIST_EXPORT=1: at boot, before anything is built, the console's own record files
of this shader folder go to pipeline_export.list beside them (written beside, renamed over).

EDEN_UP_PIPELINE_LIST_IMPORT=1 (pipeline_import.list in the shader folder) or =<path>: at boot,
before anything is built, each program's code is looked up by its hash in this console's own
record files and in the shader set file made from the player's own game (prep_shader_set.bin,
layouts edenset3 and the older edenset2: VideoCommon::ShaderSet::ForEachProgramCode). The list's
records whose code was all found, that this console has no record of, that this device's dynamic
state can draw (OtherDeviceBits) and that were made with this driver are written back whole:
prep_imported.bin, prep_imported_mesh.bin, prep_imported_compute.bin. EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP's
preparation reads the first two as predicted records (translated on the workers before play,
built once so the driver's disk cache holds them, kept; task/mesh ones, which run as compute,
are built and remembered, not kept); the boot builds the compute ones like its own. One log line
gives every count. prep_imported.stamp keeps the files as they are while the list, the shader
set file, this device's dynamic states and key switches (ShaderSetDeviceIdentity) and (unless
all code was found) the own record files are unchanged. A list that is
gone, or not a list of this build, takes the three files away.
EDEN_UP_PIPELINE_LIST_IMPORT_DRIVER=1: a record made with another driver version is taken with
this device's driver fields; without it such records are counted and left out.

Checks on every list record: a known kind, 1-6 programs, compute exactly one compute program,
graphics as many programs as the key has hashes, task/mesh kind only with a task or mesh
program, each program's bytes as long as FileEnvironment::RecordTailSize (new, from the head
alone) says, code at most 16 MiB, each program's code hash XOR the native tag one of the key's
program hashes (not for a task/mesh record's mesh-state slots), and found code of the same hash
and size (checked again when it is copied back). A bad record is counted and left out; a list
that cannot be read on stops there. With _DRIVER=1 two records that become one key are written
once. Host check (t154/host): the console's records rebuilt from a list are byte for byte the
original records (1,346 + 2,975 + 368 + 401 + 705 + 3,458 records, 0 differ); C++ export and
tools/pipeline-list.py export give the same bytes.

Off (both unset): one getenv in LoadDiskResources (two with EXPORT's) and one in PrepareKept,
cached; nothing read, written or logged. Not in the store stamp (the translation is unchanged),
but vk_pipeline_cache.cpp and shader_environment.cpp are inputs of the translation id (0596), so
a build with this patch gives a new id and one cold preparation when EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SOURCE_STAMP=1.

Credits: the shader set's program table and extractor this reads (T122, Fritchii's extractor);
the preparation it feeds (0567, after zortos293/Lichii#895 and #896, zmckenney).
